                <pb facs="0143" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg103"/>

                <head>[From the same.]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Extract from the
                            annual address of Mr. E. A. Leatham, M. C, delivered to the electors and
                            others, at <placeName>Huddersfield</placeName>, Tuesday</hi>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1865-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 24</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>“Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leatha</hi>. concluded with some observations on
                    the American war, upon which subject his sentiments had not changed. He regarded
                    the victories of Sherman as a ratification of the wise policy of re-electing
                    President Lincoln.”</p>
            </div>
